<title>UK: Dowa Mining sets $50 million bond with warrants.</title>
<headline>Dowa Mining sets $50 million bond with warrants.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by lead manager Nikko Europe.</p>
<p> BORROWER   DOWA MINING CO. LTD</p>
<p> GUARANTOR  THE INDUSTRIAL BANK OF JAPAN</p>
<p> AMT    $50 MLN	 COUPON     4.625     MATURITY    24 APR.01</p>
<p> TYPE   WARRANTS	ISS PRICE  PAR	 PAY DATE    24.APR.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  2.25	DENOMS (K) 10 + TWO WARRANTS</p>
<p> LISTING    LUX	 SALE LIMS  US/UK/JAPAN</p>
<p> NEG PLG    NO	  CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   IPMA 2</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ENGLISH   HOME CTRY  JAPAN     TAX PROVS   STANDARD</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.75	SELL CONC  1.50	PRAECIPUUM  0.25</p>
<p> EXERCISE PERIOD	08.MAY.97-17.APR.01</p>
<p> INDICATIVE PREMIUM   2.50 PCT</p>
<p> NOTES    WARRANTS ALLOW TO SUBSCIBE FOR DOWA MINIING COMMON</p>
<p>	    STOCK.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
